5|n|The fifth month of the Jewish year according to the ecclesiastical reckoning, the eleventh by the civil computation, coinciding nearly with August.	N:231q,58,1~231q,58,1
2h|n|The act of shortening, or reducing. ; The result of abbreviating; an abridgment. ; The form to which a word or phrase is reduced by contraction and omission; a letter or letters, standing for a word or phrase of which they are a part; as, Gen. for Genesis; U.S.A. for United States of America. ; One dash, or more, through the stem of a note, dividing it respectively into quavers, semiquavers, or demi-semiquavers.	N:tmv,62,3;17ev,52,3~17ev,52,3;tmv,62,3
