al|n|To take or withdraw (one's self) to such a distance as to prevent intercourse; -- used with the reflexive pronoun. ; To withhold from being present.	N:20bd,35,3~20bd,35,3
al|a|Being away from a place; withdrawn from a place; not present. ; Not existing; lacking; as, the part was rudimental or absent. ; Inattentive to what is passing; absent-minded; preoccupied; as, an absent air.	j:20bd,35,3~20bd,35,3
ba|n|In a plane, the two imaginary circular points at infinity; in space of three dimensions, the imaginary circle at infinity.	v:28g9,29,28;1vjg,22,6~28g9,29,28;1vjg,22,6	V:fyl,93,32;1lv7,90,37;19jz,23,1;28od,18,1~1lv7,90,37;fyl,93,32;28od,18,1;19jz,23,1	n:28g9,34,40~28g9,34,40	N:lwk,96,18;fyl,86,20;1bgu,74,32;72b,71,4;29w2,55,9;1av2,48,6;1sy7,44,4;1lv7,38,1;pwa,36,5;2byr,34,2;28od,34,3;19jm,33,2;2bw7,28,10;28o9,24,3;1cb5,20,1~1bgu,74,32;fyl,86,20;lwk,96,18;2bw7,28,10;29w2,55,9;nb0,15,6;1av2,48,6;pwa,36,5;1sy7,44,4;72b,71,4;28o9,24,3;1lv4,17,3;28od,34,3;24no,11,2;19jm,33,2
